{
  "callGas6364RetentionAcrossUpgrades": {
    "_info": {
      "comment": "EIP-150's gas-retention rule: a caller may forward at most 63/64 of what it has, keeping a 64th back so it can still act after the call returns. NOTHING in this suite asserted it before today. The probe forwards GAS -- every remaining unit it can name -- to a helper whose only instruction records how much it actually received. What the helper stores IS the rule's output.",
      "eip": "EIP-150 at Gas Reprice.",
      "whyNoOtherFixtureReachedIt": "Ten fixtures here execute a CALL, so the opcode is well covered. Only one names an explicit gas figure, and it requests a FIXED 10,000 -- far below the 63/64 cap, so the cap never binds and the rule never runs. Executing an opcode is not the same as exercising the rule that governs it, and that distinction is the whole finding.",
      "slots": "0x1f on the probe is the liveness marker. The measurement is NOT on the probe: it is slot 0 of the helper at 0x5000, written by the helper itself, so the post-state root carries it.",
      "theDiscriminator": "A client that forwards everything instead of 63/64 hands the helper a larger number, the helper stores that larger number, and the root moves. There is no way to satisfy this fixture without implementing the retention.",
      "provenance": "Authored 2026-08-25 after a wrong-build matrix found that a client which forwards all available gas -- EIP-150's rule simply absent -- was passed silently by all 36 state fixtures then in the suite. It was the most serious of the four gaps that matrix found: a foundational 2016 consensus rule that every later fork inherits.",
      "oracle": "core-geth's own statetest runner, which is not the implementation under certification.",
      "oracle-version": "core-geth modernized 1.13.0-26975d6a. Production v1.12.21 cannot be used: its t8n fork table has no ETC_DieHard, ETC_Gotham or ETC_DefuseDifficultyBomb.",
      "generated": "2026-08-25",
      "signing": "txbytes carries the signed transaction. Legacy signature through Gas Reprice, replay-protected from Die Hard.",
      "unfilled-no-fork-name": "No expectation for ETC_Thanos: the generator's fork table has no name for it.",
      "unfilled-not-a-state-rule": "No expectation for ETC_DAOFork, ETC_DAOWars, ETC_FrontierThawing, ETC_MESSOff, ETC_MESSOn."
    },
